  "notes": "{盲信|もうしん} has a negative connotation, suggesting uncritical or naive acceptance of something.\n\nETYMOLOGY:\n- {盲|もう} (blind) + {信|しん} (belief)\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {妄信|もうしん}: same meaning, different kanji ({妄|もう} = delusion)\n- ⟦{信仰|しんこう}→信仰：03685_shinkou⟧: faith, belief (neutral)\n- ⟦{心酔|しんすい}→心酔：09238_shinsui⟧: infatuation, devotion (less negative)\n- ⟦{鵜呑|うの}み→鵜呑み：27228_unomi⟧⟦に→に：00314_ni⟧⟦する→する：00392_suru⟧: to swallow whole, believe uncritically\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {盲信|もうしん}⟦して→する：00392_suru⟧⟦は→は：00079_ha⟧いけない: one shouldn't blindly believe\n- {盲信|もうしん}⟦{者|しゃ}→〜者：04662_sha⟧: a blind believer",
